{"seq":7,"slug":"materials-science","title":"材料科学","stage":"DONE","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science","introMarkdown":"# 材料科学 简介\n\n材料科学研究物质的内部结构如何决定其宏观性能。为什么钢铁坚硬而橡胶柔软？为什么同样是碳原子，石墨可以用来写字而金刚石却能切割玻璃？这些问题的答案都藏在原子排列和微观组织的细节之中。材料科学的核心任务，就是建立\"成分—加工—结构—性能\"这四者之间的因果链条。\n\n对于自学者而言，材料科学的入门门槛在于它需要同时调用物理、化学和力学的知识。但好消息是，这门学科有一条清晰的主线：先理解晶体结构和相图这两个最基本的概念工具，然后就可以用它们去解释和预测各类材料的行为。\n\n本学习空间将材料科学的知识体系组织为四个章节。**第一章 材料基础** 从晶体结构出发，介绍相图的阅读与应用以及扩散动力学，为后续各类材料的学习奠定微观基础。**第二章 金属材料** 以钢铁和有色金属为主要对象，讨论合金设计原理、变形强化机制和腐蚀防护方法。**第三章 高分子与陶瓷** 进入非金属材料的世界，涵盖高分子科学、陶瓷材料和复合材料，它们在轻量化和耐高温等领域正发挥越来越重要的作用。**第四章 功能材料** 关注材料的电学、生物学和纳米尺度特性，介绍电子材料、生物材料和纳米材料等前沿方向。\n\n材料科学非常适合结合实物来学习。建议在阅读每个章节时，思考身边常见物品的材料选择——手机外壳为什么用铝合金或陶瓷，运动鞋底为什么用特定的高分子——这种联系实际的习惯能帮助你真正理解材料选择背后的工程逻辑。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"materials-fundamentals","title":"材料基础","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/materials-fundamentals","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"crystal-structure","title":"大学材料科学 — 晶体结构","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/materials-fundamentals/crystal-structure"},{"seq":2,"slug":"defects-diffusion","title":"大学材料科学 — 晶体缺陷与扩散","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/materials-fundamentals/defects-diffusion"},{"seq":3,"slug":"phase-diagrams","title":"大学材料科学 — 相图","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/materials-fundamentals/phase-diagrams"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"metallic-materials","title":"金属材料","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/metallic-materials","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"steel-alloys","title":"大学材料科学 — 钢铁与合金钢","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/metallic-materials/steel-alloys"},{"seq":2,"slug":"non-ferrous-metals","title":"大学材料科学 — 有色金属","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/metallic-materials/non-ferrous-metals"},{"seq":3,"slug":"heat-treatment","title":"大学材料科学 — 热处理","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/metallic-materials/heat-treatment"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"polymers-ceramics","title":"高分子与陶瓷","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/polymers-ceramics","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"polymer-science","title":"大学材料科学 — 高分子科学","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/polymers-ceramics/polymer-science"},{"seq":2,"slug":"ceramics","title":"大学材料科学 — 陶瓷材料","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/polymers-ceramics/ceramics"},{"seq":3,"slug":"composites","title":"大学材料科学 — 复合材料","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/polymers-ceramics/composites"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"functional-materials","title":"功能材料","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/functional-materials","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"semiconductor-materials","title":"大学材料科学 — 半导体材料","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/functional-materials/semiconductor-materials"},{"seq":2,"slug":"magnetic-materials","title":"大学材料科学 — 磁性材料","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/functional-materials/magnetic-materials"},{"seq":3,"slug":"nanomaterials","title":"大学材料科学 — 纳米材料","url":"/education/university/engineering/materials-science/functional-materials/nanomaterials"}]}]}